Themes, keybindings, preview/cancel state, cursor style, image-render preferences, Mermaid display options and other pure appearance/interaction state belong in src/ava/tui, app/tui or tui-named files, tui-thread-only without locks/UnlockedData. Do not create canonical theme, keybinding, preview or draft domains. Draft text remains frontend-only until submitted as a string. Classify ambiguous settings by actual effect: model variant/reasoning affecting execution is backend state, reasoning display is UI-only; attachment authority is backend-owned, image visibility/rendering is local. Keep external service capabilities separate from local preferences and backend authority. Preserve approved settings persistence, precedence and actionable reload failures without making persistence alone a reason for UnlockedData.

Reload publishes changed backend facts and applies UI-only changes in their local owner, preserving unchanged/success/failure, preview/cancel and prior valid state on failure. Remove obsolete migrated fields and redundant result payloads, retaining narrow errors/control. Verify trust/resource changes, settings reload, theme preview/persistence, image/cursor/Mermaid behavior and overview transitions with deterministic tests and relevant terminal smokes. Existing history/streaming transport remains the explicit deferred exception and is not redesigned by settings work.

Use /05/01/05/Result.md as the disposition matrix. Preserve deferred image/editor/Mermaid and other interactive service APIs and their existing synchronization; local rendering preferences themselves remain tui-thread-only. The direct set_tui_config_theme calls are corrected by frontend ownership/dispatch, not by canonical backend theme publication or banning legitimate calls from frontend code under app/tui. Local keybinding reload also updates local help/palette hints; remove backend catalog dependence on presentation-only hotkeys. Do not require a new general reload/revision protocol for single-thread-owned settings. Keep protocol-specific pending/status fields outside this goal until the user's first-popup design exists.

The resource-overview portion requires a concrete supplementary type proposal and user approval before implementation, separately from already-approved local settings work. Specify exact safe resource groups/names/counts/lower bounds, filtering, copy bounds and backend publication owner; decide whether to copy existing safe facts or use a backend-prepared summary. Do not copy raw context/freshness vectors, source paths, agent instructions or prompt bodies. Preserve the approved nested PromptModeAndContextSources_ts inside unwrapped ResolvedPromptState: frontend PromptModeAndContextSources copies only mode and context_sources.size(), with known zero for an empty vector and no duplicate backend count. Same-size source changes may notify without changing the displayed count.

